## COMMUNICATION
Zr-based mesoporous MOFs with uniform mesochannels and crystallized microporous framework were constructed in a water-based system using amphoteric surfactants as templates. Amphoteric surfactant not only produced a hexagonal cylindrical mesophase but also offered a coordinating agent chemically anchoring to the metal precursor for the directed crystallization of MOFs along surfactant assemblies.
